pected margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; fundamentals point clearly one way (post-redistricting), so it is treated as safe for that party.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Cleo Fields (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Louisiana's 6th District is an open seat after Democrat Cleo Fields retired to run for state senate. The redrawn district leans Republican by about 16 points, and six Republicans are on the ballot alongside two Democrats and a Libertarian. State Senator Blake Miguez leads the Republican field with roughly $7.6 million raised and $2.1 million on hand, far outpacing every other candidate.\n\nThe Democratic nominees, Pat Forbes and Lindsay Garcia, have raised modest sums with little cash remaining, and no significant outside spending has materialized on either side. A single registered-voter poll put the Democrat at 27%, and prediction markets price a Republican win around 93%. The fundamentals, money, and market pricing all align on a Republican hold in this Baton Rouge–area seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.024, "margin": -16.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0303, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0083, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0276, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0147, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0333, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0144, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0284, "margi